---
title: "Signal -- Time Saved on Upgrades | 4DA"
description: "Free 4DA finds every version-confirmed vulnerability on your machine and names the fix. Signal adds the Upgrade Plan, the full worklist and full history. $12/mo or $99/yr."
permalink: "/signal.html"
---
{% extends "base.njk" %}

{% block head %}
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://4da.ai/signal">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Signal -- Time Saved on Upgrades">
  <meta property="og:description" content="The Upgrade Plan, the full Preemption worklist and full history, on top of free version-confirmed findings and fixes. $12/mo.">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://4da.ai/signal">
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://4da.ai/og-image.png">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="Signal -- Time Saved on Upgrades">
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="The Upgrade Plan, the full Preemption worklist and full history, on top of free version-confirmed findings and fixes.">
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://4da.ai/og-image.png">

  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
    :root {
      --bg: #0A0A0A; --bg-card: #141414; --bg-hover: #1A1A1A; --bg-depth: #0E0E0E;
      --text: #FFFFFF; --text-secondary: #A0A0A0; --text-muted: #666;
      --accent: #F97316; --accent-dim: rgba(249,115,22,0.08); --accent-border: rgba(249,115,22,0.15);
      --border: #2A2A2A; --success: #22C55E; --radius: 12px;
    }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    body { font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
    code, .mono { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
    a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
    a:hover { opacity: 0.8; }
    .container { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }

    /* Nav */
    .nav { height: 56px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); background: rgba(10,10,10,0.95); backdrop-filter: blur(12px); position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100; }
    .nav-inner { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; height: 100%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; }
    .nav-brand { font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
    .nav-brand img { width: 24px; height: 24px; border-radius: 50%; opacity: 0.8; }
    .nav-links { display: flex; gap: 24px; }
    .nav-links a { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 14px; }
    .nav-links a:hover { color: var(--text); opacity: 1; }

    /* Hero */
    .hero { padding: 100px 0 40px; text-align: center; }
    .hero-label { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 20px; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 52px); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin-bottom: 20px; }
    .hero h1 span { color: var(--accent); }
    .hero .hero-sub { font-size: 18px; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 32px; line-height: 1.7; }
    .hero .hero-technical { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.8; padding: 20px 24px; background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; text-align: left; }
    .hero .hero-technical .comment { color: #4A6A4A; }
    .hero .hero-technical .key { color: var(--accent); }
    .hero .hero-technical .val { color: #A0A0A0; }

    .divider { border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 0; }

    /* Already Free */
    .already-free { padding: 60px 0 40px; }
    .section-label { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px; text-align: center; }
    .section-title { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 12px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .section-sub { font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); text-align: center; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto 36px; line-height: 1.7; }
    .free-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr)); gap: 8px; max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .free-item { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 6px 0; }
    .free-item::before { content: "// "; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; }
    .free-highlight { color: var(--text-secondary); font-weight: 500; }

    /* Signal Features */
    .signal-section { padding: 60px 0; }
    .signal-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
    .feature-card { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 28px 28px 24px; transition: border-color 0.3s; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
    .feature-card:hover { border-color: var(--accent-border); }
    .feature-card .tag { display: inline-block; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-dim); padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .feature-card h3 { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
    .feature-card .scenario { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .feature-card .technical { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 10px 14px; background: var(--bg-depth); border-radius: 6px; line-height: 1.6; }
    .feature-card .technical span { color: var(--accent); }

    /* Two-column layout for feature cards */
    .signal-grid-2col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 20px; }

    /* Compound section */
    .compound { padding: 60px 0; }
    .compound-content { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .compound-phases { margin-top: 32px; }
    .phase { padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .phase:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
    .phase-header { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
    .phase-label { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; flex-shrink: 0; }
    .phase-title { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; }
    .phase-desc { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 72px; }

    /* How it works */
    .how-it-works { padding: 60px 0; }
    .how-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px; margin-top: 32px; }
    .how-card { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 24px; }
    .how-card .step { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 8px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
    .how-card h4 { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 6px; }
    .how-card p { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }

    /* Data sovereignty callout */
    .sovereignty { padding: 48px 0; }
    .sovereignty-box { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--accent-border); border-radius: 16px; padding: 32px 40px; max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .sovereignty-box h3 { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .sovereignty-box p { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .sovereignty-box p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .sovereignty-box .highlight { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

    /* Pricing */
    .pricing { padding: 60px 0; text-align: center; }
    .pricing-title { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .pricing-sub { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 32px; }

    .toggle { display: inline-flex; background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 3px; margin-bottom: 32px; }
    .toggle button { padding: 8px 24px; border: none; background: transparent; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; border-radius: 6px; cursor: pointer; transition: all 0.2s; }
    .toggle button.active { background: var(--accent); color: #000; }
    .save-badge { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; color: var(--success); margin-left: 4px; }
    /* On the orange active pill the green badge read at ~1.2:1; black matches the button label (~7.5:1). */
    .toggle button.active .save-badge { color: #000; font-weight: 600; }

    .price-card { background: var(--bg-card); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 16px; padding: 40px; max-width: 440px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .price-amount { font-size: 48px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
    .price-amount .currency { font-size: 20px; color: var(--text-secondary); vertical-align: top; margin-right: 2px; }
    .price-amount .period { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }
    .price-annual-note { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 8px 0 20px; min-height: 20px; }
    .price-math { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 24px; padding: 10px 16px; background: var(--bg-depth); border-radius: 6px; text-align: left; }
    .price-math span { color: var(--accent); }
    .price-btn { display: block; width: 100%; padding: 14px; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; border: none; border-radius: 10px; cursor: pointer; transition: all 0.2s; background: var(--accent); color: #000; }
    .price-btn:hover { opacity: 0.9; transform: translateY(-1px); }
    .price-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: wait; }
    .price-trial { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 12px; }

    .price-features { text-align: left; margin-top: 24px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .price-features li { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding: 4px 0; list-style: none; }
    .price-features li::before { content: "\2713 "; color: var(--success); font-weight: 700; margin-right: 6px; }

    /* FAQ */
    .faq { padding: 60px 0; }
    .faq-title { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .faq-item { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 20px 0; }
    .faq-item:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .faq-q { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .faq-a { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
    .faq-a code { font-size: 12px; background: var(--bg-card); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }

    /* Footer */
    footer { padding: 48px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); text-align: center; }
    footer p { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); }
    footer a { color: var(--text-muted); }
    footer a:hover { color: var(--text); }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .signal-grid-2col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .how-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .free-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
      .price-card { padding: 28px; }
      .sovereignty-box { padding: 24px; }
      .phase-desc { padding-left: 0; margin-top: 4px; }
    }
  </style>
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
  <nav class="nav">
    <div class="nav-inner">
      <a href="/" class="nav-brand"><img src="hero-sun.jpg" alt="4DA">4DA</a>
      <div class="nav-links">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/merch">Merch</a>
        <a href="/streets">STREETS</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- ==================== HERO ==================== -->
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-label">4DA Signal</div>
      <h1>Free tells you what's wrong.<br>Signal <span>saves you the upgrade work</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Free 4DA finds every version-confirmed vulnerability across the projects on your machine and names the version that fixes it. Signal turns those findings into an ordered Upgrade Plan, adds the full Preemption worklist, and keeps your full history.</p>
      <div class="hero-technical">
        <div><span class="comment">// what signal does in a sentence</span></div>
        <div><span class="key">input</span>:&nbsp; <span class="val">every lockfile on your machine &times; OSV advisories &times; registry releases</span></div>
        <div><span class="key">output</span>: <span class="val">one ordered upgrade plan, the full worklist, full history</span></div>
        <div><span class="key">delta</span>:&nbsp; <span class="val">the planning on top of free findings and fixes</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- ==================== FREE TIER ==================== -->
  <section class="already-free">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">Already included free</div>
      <div class="section-title">Every vulnerability and its fix is free.</div>
      <p class="section-sub">Dependabot, OSV-Scanner and npm audit give individual developers vulnerability alerts for free, and so does 4DA. No trial. No account. No expiration.</p>
      <div class="free-grid">
        <div class="free-item free-highlight">Version-confirmed findings, every local project</div>
        <div class="free-item free-highlight">The fix version for each finding</div>
        <div class="free-item free-highlight">The daily Brief</div>
        <div class="free-item free-highlight">Open MCP server (16 tools)</div>
        <div class="free-item">Upgrade impact for your agent</div>
        <div class="free-item">Upgrade planning for your agent</div>
        <div class="free-item">Install-drift checks</div>
        <div class="free-item">CLI binary</div>
        <div class="free-item">Developer news, scored</div>
        <div class="free-item">Natural language search (BYOK)</div>
        <div class="free-item">30 days of history</div>
        <div class="free-item">Local-first (BYOK for cloud AI)</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- ==================== SIGNAL FEATURES ==================== -->
  <section class="signal-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">What Signal adds</div>
      <div class="section-title">Time saved on upgrades.</div>
      <p class="section-sub">Everything below runs on your machine, reads the same lockfiles as the free tier, and uses your own API key wherever an AI model is involved.</p>

      <!-- Primary Features (full-width) -->
      <div class="signal-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="tag">Upgrade Plan</span>
          <h3>Every fix across your projects, in one order</h3>
          <p class="scenario">Twelve findings across five repositories are twelve tabs of advisories. The Upgrade Plan collapses them into steps, one per package, most actionable first: the version that clears every advisory on it, per release line, with major-version jumps flagged. When the vulnerable copy is transitive, it names the parent package that brings it in and, where one of your own projects already resolved a newer parent, which version of it clears the advisory. Where the lockfile records the requirement, it says when a lockfile refresh is enough.</p>
          <div class="technical"><span>plan</span> = version-confirmed matches &times; your dependency edges &times; installed versions in every project</div>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="tag">Full worklist</span>
          <h3>More than the version-confirmed floor</h3>
          <p class="scenario">The free tier shows the findings OSV confirms against your installed versions. Signal adds the rest of the Preemption worklist: findings an AI model has assessed against your stack, and early-warning chains assembled from releases and discussions about the packages you depend on. Each one says how confident it is and why.</p>
          <div class="technical"><span>worklist</span> = version-confirmed floor + AI-assessed findings + early-warning chains</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="signal-grid-2col">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="tag">History</span>
          <h3>Full history, and watches</h3>
          <p class="scenario">The free tier keeps the last 30 days. Signal keeps everything, and adds standing queries and package watches that check new items against what you asked to follow.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="tag">Coverage</span>
          <h3>Blind Spots and Knowledge Gaps</h3>
          <p class="scenario">Supporting views over the same inventory: the dependencies you rely on but have no coverage of (with an optional AI assessment), and the dependencies with upstream changes you have not engaged with.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- ==================== DATA SOVEREIGNTY ==================== -->
  <section class="sovereignty">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sovereignty-box">
        <h3>Your data stays yours. Always.</h3>
        <p>Signal runs 100% locally. Your lockfiles, your history, your Developer DNA, your Knowledge Gaps &mdash; none of it touches our servers. <span class="highlight">The license key is the only network call Signal makes to us.</span></p>
        <p>AI features use your own API keys (BYOK). Anthropic, OpenAI, or Ollama for fully local inference. We never see your prompts. We never see the responses. We are <span class="highlight">architecturally unable</span> to access your data.</p>
        <p>Cancel your subscription and your data stays. Your history, your Developer DNA, everything 4DA has gathered &mdash; all of it remains on your machine. We unlock the planning and analysis views. The data is always yours.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- ==================== HOW IT WORKS ==================== -->
  <section class="how-it-works">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">Under the hood</div>
      <div class="section-title">For developers who want to know how.</div>
      <div class="how-grid">
        <div class="how-card">
          <div class="step">01 / Inventory</div>
          <h4>Every lockfile, every project</h4>
          <p>Cargo.lock, package-lock.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, yarn.lock, poetry.lock, requirements.txt and go.mod, with early Gemfile.lock and composer.lock support. Exact installed versions, direct and transitive, stored in SQLite on your machine.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="how-card">
          <div class="step">02 / Matching</div>
          <h4>Version-confirmed against OSV</h4>
          <p>Advisories come from OSV.dev; package names go out, your code never does. A finding is raised only when your installed version is inside the affected range, and it is scoped by dev-only, transitive and per-platform reachability.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="how-card">
          <div class="step">03 / Planning</div>
          <h4>The Upgrade Plan (Signal)</h4>
          <p>Findings grouped per package, ranked, and joined with your dependency edges to name the parent upgrade or lockfile refresh. Deterministic: no AI model decides a plan step.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- ==================== PRICING ==================== -->
  <section class="pricing" id="pricing">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">Pricing</div>
      <div class="pricing-title">One tier. No gotchas.</div>
      <p class="pricing-sub">Every vulnerability and its fix stays free. Signal is for developers who want the upgrade work planned for them.</p>

      <div class="toggle">
        <button id="toggle-monthly" onclick="setPlan('monthly')">Monthly</button>
        <button id="toggle-annual" class="active" onclick="setPlan('annual')">Annual <span class="save-badge">SAVE $45</span></button>
        <button id="toggle-lifetime" onclick="setPlan('lifetime')">Lifetime</button>
      </div>

      <div class="price-card">
        <div class="price-amount">
          <span class="currency">$</span><span id="price-value">99</span><span class="period" id="price-period">/yr</span>
        </div>
        <div class="price-annual-note" id="annual-note">$8.25/mo billed annually</div>
        <div class="price-math" id="price-math">
          <span>$99</span> / 12 months = <span>$8.25/mo</span> &mdash; save $45/yr
        </div>
        <button class="price-btn" id="checkout-btn" onclick="startCheckout()">Subscribe to Signal</button>
        <div class="price-trial">14-day free trial included in the app. No credit card required to try.</div>
        <ul class="price-features">
          <li>Everything in the free tier</li>
          <li>The in-app Upgrade Plan</li>
          <li>The full Preemption worklist</li>
          <li>Full history, standing queries and package watches</li>
          <li>Blind Spots + AI assessment, Knowledge Gaps</li>
          <li>Priority support</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:24px;">All prices in AUD, tax included &mdash; checkout shows your local currency. Cancel anytime. No 4DA server — your data stays on your machine (a cloud model, if you use one, sees only what you send it).</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- ==================== FAQ ==================== -->
  <section class="faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="faq-title">Questions</div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">What's the difference between free and Signal?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Free gives you every version-confirmed vulnerability finding across the projects on your machine, the version that fixes each one, the daily Brief, the open MCP server (including upgrade impact and upgrade planning for your coding agent), the CLI, developer news scored against your stack, and 30 days of history. Signal adds the in-app Upgrade Plan, the full Preemption worklist beyond the version-confirmed floor, full history with standing queries and package watches, and Blind Spots and Knowledge Gaps as supporting views. Free tells you what is wrong and what fixes it. Signal plans the upgrade work.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Wait, the Brief is free?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Yes. The daily Brief is in the free tier: a template Brief that needs no AI model, or an AI-written one with your own API key (BYOK) or local Ollama. Vulnerability alerts are free for individual developers from Dependabot, OSV-Scanner and npm audit too; we see no reason to charge for knowing your own stack is exposed.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">What happens to my data?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Nothing extra. 4DA runs on your machine; Signal features use your own API keys (BYOK) to call AI models, so the snippets analyzed go to your chosen provider, not to us. The license key is the only thing that touches our servers.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Do I need an API key?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">No. Vulnerability findings, fix versions, the Upgrade Plan and the template Brief work without any API key. AI-powered features (the AI-written Brief, AI assessment of findings and blind spots, natural language search) need an LLM provider: OpenAI, Anthropic, or Ollama for fully local inference. You provide your own key in settings. We never see or store it.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Why does Signal cost money if it uses my API key?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Your API key powers the models. Signal is the planning built on top &mdash; the Upgrade Plan that joins findings with your dependency edges, the fuller worklist, the history. The Upgrade Plan itself is deterministic and needs no API key at all.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Can I try before subscribing?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Yes. 4DA includes a 14-day free trial of all Signal features. No credit card required. Install the app, enable Signal features, and evaluate against your real projects.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">What if I cancel?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Cancel anytime yourself from the <a href="{{ billing.portalUrl }}" rel="noopener">customer portal</a> &mdash; sign in with your purchase email; the same place updates your card and has your invoices. Your license remains valid until the end of the billing period. After that, you revert to the free tier. No data is lost &mdash; your history, your Developer DNA and everything 4DA has gathered stay on your machine. Free findings and fixes keep working; you lose access to the Signal views.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
